# `read-path`, not `get`. The public wrapper (code/environment/path.tree) declares `get`, and names are
# PACKAGE-GLOBAL in Term, so a public task and its native implementation sharing a name unify into one
# symbol: wiring them emitted `function get1(kind) { return get1(kind) }`, an infinite recursion. That is
# why this module and twelve like it declared an API and bound nothing for six months. The convention that
# works is the one code/environment.tree already uses, where the native names are `current-directory` and
# `get-variable` and cannot collide with the `directory` and `variable` they implement.

# Standard user folders. Forwards to the linked folder runtime shim, which holds the per-host layout rules.
# Internal: reached only through the public environment API.

dock load
  load <global:folder>, name folder

task read-path
  take kind, like text
  like text

  fork case, read kind
    case home
      send back
        call folder/home
    case temporary
      send back
        call folder/temporary
    case data
      send back
        call folder/data
    case configuration
      send back
        call folder/configuration
    case cache
      send back
        call folder/cache
